                <pb facs="0624" n="613" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg613"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.90H/40: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-27T11:00:00+03:25">December 27, 1937—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>131. Personal for Murray. Arrival of new Afghan Ambassador here would afford
                    suitable opportunity to mention to him third paragraph of your 43, September 4,
                    3 p.m., provided your plans are taking shape.</p>
                <p>I have not yet referred to your proposed visit to Teheran as it would undoubtedly
                    be interpreted as in the nature of a special mission.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
